ashley: opened a docs PR to add a compact tracing-hook example + cost/latency note. PR: github.com/redwood/docs/pull/842 (preview link will be in the thread).

mike: taking a look now. are you trying to keep the example framework-agnostic?

ashley: yes, minimal Node snippet that uses @redwood/inference-sdk tracer. main issue I hit: example span names don't line up with what Console groups by.

sara: paste the snippet in, will scan for the obvious mismatch.

ashley: ```js
const {Tracer} = require('@redwood/inference-sdk');
const tracer = new Tracer({service: 'console-demo'});
app.post('/invoke', async (req, res) => {
  const span = tracer.startSpan('handler');
  await runtime.request(req.body);
  span.end();
  res.sendStatus(200);
});
```

mike: yep, Console groups traces by route and model metadata. change to startSpan(`route:${req.path}`) and add span.setTag('model', modelId) so the dashboard picks up the row.

ashley: makes sense. I'll update snippet. Also found a broken internal link in the cost examples pointing at /console/dashboards/cost-breakdown — site now uses /console/observability/cost-breakdown; will fix.

ryan: good catch. small UX note: in the cost/latency guide we show p99 as text; we should show both human label and the PromQL style (quantile(0.99, ...)) so SREs can copy queries.

ashley: adding both variants and a one-line migration note: "If you previously used tracer.startSpan('handler'), change to tracer.startSpan(`route:${req.path}`) and set span.setTag('model', modelId') to preserve existing dashboard groupings." Want to include a Private deployment caveat?

mike: yes: "Private deployments: ensure OTLP/tracing collector endpoint is reachable from the customer's VPC." short and actionable.

ashley: done. also adding a tiny test snippet showing how prefix caching reduces repeated tokens and how that affects exported trace sizes (support asked for that).

sara: can you add a console screenshot of the trace grouping? even a small annotated image helps. If you can't host an image, add the expected row labels example.

ashley: adding a mock table example of the trace rows: `route:/invoke | model:gpt-lite | avg latency | cost` so we avoid including static images.

ryan: once you push updates ping me. I'll run the preview, check the dashboard grouping and the cost widget.

docs-bot: Preview site build for pull/842 queued. Status: pending (https://ci.redwood.dev/builds/59812).

ashley: pushed changes to branch, PR updated.

docs-bot: Preview updated: https://preview.docs.redwood.dev/pull/842 (checks running).

ryan: preview looks good, route names show correctly and cost widget renders with the new PromQL sample. I spotted an inline code style issue in the snippet (missing backtick around modelId) — fixed in a tiny commit.

ashley: thanks, merging once CI green.

mike: nice. i'll notify support so they can close the related ticket.

ashley: merged and released to docs site. closing thread. :tada:
